Name:           slate-to-ucs
Version:        @VERSION@
Release:        1%{?dist}
Summary:        Label sound effects with UCS metadata
License:        MIT
URL:            https://github.com/SoundsLikeJonny/Slate-To-UCS
Source0:        slate-to-ucs-%{version}.tar.gz
BuildArch:      @ARCH@
Requires:       glibc

%description
Slate-To-UCS reads a sound effect, transcribes any spoken slate and suggests
Universal Category System metadata for it: category, subcategory, CatID,
keywords and a UCS file name.

Everything runs locally. The classifier is served on loopback and offline mode
is the default, so no audio, transcript or file name leaves the machine.

%prep
%setup -q

%build
# Nothing to build: the payload is the staged tree, produced by stage.sh.

%install
mkdir -p %{buildroot}
cp -R usr %{buildroot}/

%files
/usr/bin/slate
/usr/lib/slate
/usr/share/applications/slate.desktop
/usr/share/metainfo/io.github.soundslikejonny.SlateToUCS.metainfo.xml
/usr/share/icons/hicolor/256x256/apps/slate.png
/usr/share/doc/slate/LICENSE
/usr/share/doc/slate/README.md

%changelog
* Sat Nov 14 2026 Jon Evans <jonnythejet@gmail.com> - @VERSION@-1
- First packaged release.
